WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.089
Wind has speed, direction, variation, and vertical structure.

00:00:04.089 --> 00:00:10.759
Average wind alone can hide gusts that briefly exceed a small drone's control margin.

00:00:10.759 --> 00:00:17.860
Compare forecast and observed conditions with manufacturer guidance, payload effects, operator experience, and planned altitude.

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:20.658
Structures and terrain disturb airflow.

00:00:20.658 --> 00:00:27.329
Buildings can create rotors, downwash, acceleration around corners, and turbulence on the downwind side.

00:00:27.329 --> 00:00:34.430
Trees, ridges, cliffs, and shorelines can produce localized movement that differs from an open-area reading.

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:38.088
Plan the outbound and return legs together.

00:00:38.088 --> 00:00:46.480
A favorable tailwind leaving the site may become a strong headwind during return, increasing power use and time.

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:51.429
Reserve battery for wind change, route adjustment, approach, and landing.

00:00:51.429 --> 00:00:55.948
Wind normally increases with height and can shift direction.

00:00:55.948 --> 00:01:01.328
Conditions at the launch point may not describe the mission altitude.

00:01:01.328 --> 00:01:09.290
Watch groundspeed, aircraft attitude, position-hold effort, power use, and control response for signs that margins are narrowing.

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:11.657
Payloads change wind sensitivity.

00:01:11.657 --> 00:01:19.619
A larger camera, guard, mapping attachment, or unusual center of gravity can increase drag and reduce endurance.

00:01:19.619 --> 00:01:26.290
Manufacturer maximums are not operational targets; terrain, gusts, and mission complexity justify additional margin.

00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:31.669
Use conservative go or no-go criteria and an early return point.

00:01:31.669 --> 00:01:42.644
If the aircraft struggles to hold position, battery use rises unexpectedly, or turbulence degrades control or imagery, end the mission before recovery becomes difficult.
